description:
In repos/activity-api/src/lib/posterior-update.ts, make exactly ONE edit: replace the following THREE consecutive lines with the TWELVE lines given below. The three original lines are reproduced unchanged at the top; the change is purely that the closing brace gains an `else` branch.

REPLACE these three consecutive lines, verbatim:
      task_count: Array.isArray(trace.tasks) ? trace.tasks.length : 0,
    });
  }

WITH these twelve lines, verbatim:
      task_count: Array.isArray(trace.tasks) ? trace.tasks.length : 0,
    });
  } else {
    logger.info('posterior variant update APPLIED', {
      activity_id: activityId,
      reach_verdict: reachVerdict,
      tier_class: tierClass,
      alpha_delta: alphaDelta,
      beta_delta: betaDelta,
    });
  }

ANCHORING: the line `      task_count: Array.isArray(trace.tasks) ? trace.tasks.length : 0,` occurs EXACTLY ONCE in this file, and it is the last property of the object passed to the existing `logger.info('posterior variant update SKIPPED', {...})` call. That call site is also the only occurrence of the string 'posterior variant update' in the entire file. Anchor on the task_count line; the two lines after it are the object-literal close and the if-block close.

WHY. This `if` is the decision point where the learning loop either moves a Thompson posterior or declines to. It logs ONLY the declining branch. There is no log line anywhere in this file for the branch that actually applies a posterior delta — grep confirms 'posterior variant update' appears at exactly one site, inside the skip block.

MEASURED CONSEQUENCE, 2026-09-11, a six-hour window on the live substrate. The activity-api journal contains 4268 'posterior variant update SKIPPED' lines and ZERO lines recording an applied update. The skips break down as reason=reach_ungraded 2756 and reason=all_deterministic 1512. Those are real numbers, and they are useless, because there is no denominator: it is impossible to tell from the logs whether 4268 skips accompanied 4300 decisions or 400000. Answering the simplest question one can ask about the learning loop — what fraction of posterior decisions actually move a belief — required leaving the logs entirely and counting rows in variant_performance_metrics by updated_at, which measures distinct arms touched rather than decisions taken and so cannot answer the question either.

THE GENERAL RULE THIS ENCODES: a branch that logs only its refusal produces a numerator with no denominator. Rates are the unit in which learning behaviour is judged, and a rate needs both branches instrumented. This is the same defect class as a provider-construction loop that logs every provider it built and says nothing about the ones it skipped — there, the fix was to log the skipped branch; here, the fix is to log the taken branch.

The new message deliberately mirrors the existing one field-for-field on the fields that make the two comparable — activity_id, reach_verdict, tier_class, alpha_delta, beta_delta — so the two line types can be counted against each other directly without normalising anything. It omits has_tags and task_count, which exist on the skip line specifically to diagnose WHY a skip happened and carry no information once the update applied.

This is purely additive: the `if` condition is untouched, the skip branch is byte-for-byte unchanged, and the new `else` runs only where previously nothing ran at all. No control flow changes and nothing downstream of this block is affected. All identifiers used are already in scope at this point in the function: logger, activityId, reachVerdict, tierClass, alphaDelta, betaDelta. This cannot change any type. [RETRY CONTEXT — this is a re-attempt of the gap above; the previous compose failed. Previous failure detail, which is CONTEXT ONLY and is NOT the specification: compose for gap route-edit-82e7acc6 repeated already-recorded failure class semantic_reject: The patch does not change behavior because it adds an else branch to a different logging path without executing any new code in the case where a poste] [RETRY CONTEXT — compose for gap recommit-route-edit-82e7acc6-semantic_reject repeated already-recorded failure class syntax_break: src/lib/posterior-update.ts(1096,5): error TS1128: Declaration or statement expected.. The specification is above; this failure text is context only and is not the specification.]

